# GALEYR — website, Control Centre and restaurant portal
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env.local` is gitignored.
# NEVER commit a filled-in copy. NEVER put a real value in this file.
#
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Read this before adding anything
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Every variable prefixed VITE_ is COMPILED INTO THE BROWSER BUNDLE. It is
# readable by anyone who opens dev tools. There is no such thing as a secret
# VITE_ variable.
#
# That is fine for the values below — the publishable key authorises nothing
# on its own, and row level security is what actually protects the data.
#
# It is NOT fine for:
#   - the Supabase service_role key   (bypasses every RLS policy)
#   - any database password
#   - any payment provider secret key (sk_…)
#   - any API key without server-side restrictions
#
# Those belong in Supabase Edge Function secrets, never here.
# See PHASE0_SECURITY_INCIDENT.md for what happens when this rule slips.

# ── Supabase ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dashboard → Settings → API. The publishable/anon key, not service_role.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=YOUR_PUBLISHABLE_ANON_KEY

# ── Control room contact ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shown on every page. Must be a Mogadishu number that a real person answers —
# a UK number here is not a cosmetic bug, it is a customer who cannot get help.
VITE_CONTROL_CENTRE_TEL=+252XXXXXXXXX
VITE_CONTROL_CENTRE_DISPLAY=+252 XX XXX XXXX
VITE_CONTROL_CENTRE_EMAIL=YOUR_CONTROL_ROOM_EMAIL

# ── API base ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Empty means "talk to Supabase directly", which is the current architecture.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# ── Google Maps / Places  (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Leave BLANK unless maps are actually in use. An unrestricted key in a
# browser bundle is a bill waiting to happen.
#
# Before filling this in, in Cloud Console:
#   1. Restrict the key by HTTP referrer to your domains
#   2. Restrict it to only the APIs it needs
#   3. Set a PER-API DAILY QUOTA CAP
#
# A budget alert does not stop spending. It emails you afterwards. Only a
# quota cap stops the meter.
VITE_GOOGLE_PLACES_KEY=
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_MONTHLY_BUDGET=0
